; `range`: the counted loop, with the bound read ONCE.
;
; The shape these replace is written by hand about a hundred times in
; this repository:
;
;   (let ((mut i 0)) (while (< i (vecLen xs)) { BODY (set i (+ i 1)) }))
;
; and it re-reads `(vecLen xs)` on every iteration. That is the case
; term 4 below is about, and it is a correctness property rather than a
; speed one: a bound that reads a structure the body MUTATES is a loop
; whose length moves under it. `range` binds the bound before the loop,
; so it cannot.
;
; What each term establishes:
;
;   1. `range` over [0, n) counts [0, n) ascending, and the sum says which values
;      and in what order - 0+1+2+3+4 is 10, and no other subset of
;      0..4 sums to it by accident with the count printed beside it.
;   2. `range` with a nonzero start counts [lo, hi), so it starts where it is told and stops
;      before the end. 3+4+5+6 = 18.
;   3. An EMPTY range runs zero times, both ways round: `(range i 0 0 ..)`
;      and `(range i 5 5 ..)` and a backwards `(range i 7 3 ..)`. A
;      loop that runs once on an empty range is the off-by-one this
;      pins.
;   4. THE BOUND IS READ ONCE. The body pushes onto the very Vec the
;      bound was computed from; the loop must still run twice. Written
;      with the hand-rolled `while` this expands to, it would run until
;      the Vec ran out of memory.
;   5. The binder is the CALLER's name and the template's are renamed
;      (MAC-HYG-10): a body that mentions `cur` or `hi` - the names
;      inside the macro - means its own. Both are bound here to values
;      the loop must not disturb, and printed after it.
;   6. Nesting: the inner loop's binder shadows nothing of the outer's,
;      and both counters advance independently. 3 x 4 = 12 iterations.
(import IO)

(import Pre (range))

(import Vec)

(import Mem)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let (
    (acc (memAlloc 8))
    (v vecNew)
    (hi 111)
    (cur 222)
  )
    {
      ; --- 1. range counts [0, n) ---
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range i 0 5 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) i)))
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 10

      ; --- 2. range counts [lo, hi) ---
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range j 3 7 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) j)))
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 18

      ; --- 3. empty ranges run zero times ---
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range a 0 0 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) 1)))
      (range b 5 5 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) 1)))
      (range c 7 3 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) 1)))
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 0

      ; --- 4. the bound is read once ---
      (vecPush v 10)
      (vecPush v 20)
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range k 0 (vecLen v)
        {
          (vecPush v 99)
          (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) 1))
        })
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 2, not runaway
      (println (vecLen v))  ; 4: the body really did push

      ; --- 5. hygiene: the template's names are not the caller's ---
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range n 0 3 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) hi)))
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 333
      (println hi)  ; 111
      (println cur)  ; 222

      ; --- 6. nesting ---
      (memSetWord acc 0 0)
      (range p 0 3
        (range q 0 4 (memSetWord acc 0 (+ (memGetWord acc 0) 1))))
      (println (memGetWord acc 0))  ; 12
      0
    }
  )
)
